# Everything this repository ignores, in one file (dbmeta D58).

# The upstream checkouts, one folder for each repository that ivy ports or
# copies from. Each one is a reference, and it is never part of this
# repository. The rule has no slash at its end, so it also matches a symbolic
# link to the folder in a git worktree.
/upstream

# The Claude Code permissions of one person. The shared .claude/settings.json
# is not ignored, because a setting that belongs to the project is committed.
# See dbmeta D89.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The git worktrees in which the coding agents work. Each one is a checkout of
# this repository, and its work comes back through the main checkout.
/.claude/worktrees/

# The corpus of test files that a script downloads for the comparisons of the
# test module (D13). The corpus is fetched, not source.
/test/corpus

# The cache of the command test/cmd/review: the files of the corpus that it
# downloads, and the pages that the reference programs render.
/test/review/cache

# The workspace that points at a checkout of okage next to ivy, until okage
# tags the release that ivy needs. Each maintainer keeps their own.
/go.work
/go.work.sum
